lated vertex is a clique of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find_cliques"},{"text":", igraph ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximal_cliques"},{"text":", JGraphT’s Bron–Kerbosch finders).","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"role":"collection","title":"Cliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"type":"topic","title":"maximalCliques()","abstract":[{"text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; see ","type":"text"},{"code":"MaximalCliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"find_cliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", igraph ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximal_cliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", JGraphT’s Bron–Kerbosch finders).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"role":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s